window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-886686d95c8255a4"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"bedrock-through-litellm\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"litellm-bedrock\">通过 LiteLLM 使用 Bedrock</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面网址末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>当你的组织通过 LiteLLM 将 Codex 请求路由到 Amazon Bedrock 时，请使用本页。如果已部署 LiteLLM 网关，请先连接 Codex；只有组织需要新建网关时，才部署 LiteLLM。</p> <p>要连接现有网关，请从<a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4?anchor=connect-to-an-existing-gateway\">连接到现有网关</a>开始。要在 AWS 上部署 LiteLLM，请从<a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4?anchor=prepare-a-gateway\">准备网关</a>开始。若不通过网关直接访问，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">Amazon Bedrock</a>。</p> <p>其他网关产品也必须满足相同的<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关要求</a>，并遵循相同的 <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">API／提供商连接流程</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-to-an-existing-gateway\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">连接到现有网关</h2> <p>请向网关管理员获取以下信息：</p> <ul> <li>HTTPS 基础 URL，例如 <code>https://gateway.example.com/v1</code>。</li> <li>LiteLLM 路由到已批准 Bedrock 模型的模型别名。</li> <li>要写入 Codex 配置的提供方 ID。</li> <li>有作用范围限制的网关凭据，或能返回该凭据的身份验证辅助程序。</li> <li>组织配置中提供的任何模型目录。</li> </ul> <p>然后按以下顺序完成连接：</p> <ol> <li>请网关团队确认网关能够处理 <code>POST /v1/responses</code>、流式传输响应、保留后续轮次和工具调用，并路由已批准的别名。详情见<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a>。</li> <li>按照<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=configure-the-provider\">使用 API／提供商凭据</a>配置提供方、模型和凭据。</li> <li>核实当前启用的提供方和别名，发送连接指南中的简短 <code>gateway-ok</code> 提示词，并确认 LiteLLM 记录显示了预期用户和别名。</li> <li>如需在整个组织中分发配置，请继续阅读<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">部署网关</a>。</li> </ol> <p>网关凭据用于向 LiteLLM 验证你的身份。网关自行管理 Bedrock 凭据；你不需要将这些凭据复制到工作站上。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-a-gateway\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">准备网关</h2> <p>只有在连接 Codex 之前需要新建 LiteLLM 网关时，才使用本节。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-deploy\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">部署前准备</h3> <p>请确认你具备以下条件：</p> <ul> <li>有权限在 AWS 环境中部署已批准的 LiteLLM 架构。</li> <li>能访问将要路由的 Bedrock 模型或推理配置文件。</li> <li>已审核的 LiteLLM 镜像和部署方案。</li> <li>可信的 HTTPS 主机名和证书。</li> <li>受限的客户端网络范围。</li> </ul> <p>对于下方的 Runtime 示例，网关的 AWS 身份需要对所选推理配置文件和账户默认项目拥有 <code>bedrock:InvokeModel</code> 权限。必需权限请参阅 AWS 的 <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-6-sol.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GPT-6 Sol 设置说明（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"architecture\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">架构</h3> <p>该部署让 LiteLLM 位于 Codex 与 Bedrock 之间，并在客户端边界使用 HTTPS。负载均衡器和 LiteLLM 均位于组织的网关边界内；提供方凭据保留在网关上。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex 通过 HTTPS 负载均衡器向 LiteLLM 发送带有作用范围限制的网关凭据和 Responses API 请求。LiteLLM 将已批准的别名路由到 Amazon Bedrock，而提供方凭据保留在服务器端。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/litellm-bedrock-architecture.svg\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex 通过 HTTPS 负载均衡器向 LiteLLM 发送带有作用范围限制的网关凭据和 Responses API 请求。LiteLLM 将已批准的别名路由到 Amazon Bedrock，而提供方凭据保留在服务器端。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/litellm-bedrock-architecture.svg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>请将入站访问限制为已批准的客户端，将数据库和缓存端口保留在私有网络中，并且只授予网关所需的 Bedrock 权限。部署时请用摘要固定镜像版本，避免重启时悄悄切换实现版本。</p> <p>提示词、源文本片段和工具结果都会经过网关，并可能进入网关日志。启用请求日志前，请确定数据保留期限、访问权限和脱敏方式。MCP 服务器和插件使用独立的连接与身份验证方式；此网关配置不会替它们配置连接。</p> <p><a id=\"deployment-checkpoints\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">部署检查点</h3> <p>将网关交给开发者使用前，请按顺序完成以下检查点：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>检查点</th> <th>产出</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>部署代理，并配置私有数据库和缓存依赖。</td> <td>稳定的 HTTPS 基础 URL（以 <code>/v1</code> 结尾），并由网关管理 Bedrock 身份验证。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>配置模型路由及对应的客户端目录。</td> <td>稳定的 Codex 别名，并映射到预期的 Bedrock 目标模型。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>验证 Responses 支持。</td> <td>流式 <code>POST /v1/responses</code> 响应，并以 <code>response.completed</code> 结束。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>签发测试凭据。</td> <td>针对单个用户、仅限指定别名的虚拟密钥，且设有到期时间、预算和速率限制。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>连接一名开发者。</td> <td>已配置提供方的 Codex，以及通过网关验证成功的简短提示词。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>下方各节会介绍每个检查点。正式上线前，还要测试后续轮次、工具和凭据撤销。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-bedrock-route\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"bedrock\">选择 Bedrock 路由</h3> <p>LiteLLM 的上游路由决定 Bedrock 端点、模型标识符和身份验证方式。部署或更改网关时，请将这些配置作为一组统一管理。</p> <p>新配置应使用 Bedrock Runtime。下方示例使用其兼容 OpenAI 的 Responses 端点。</p> <p>Bedrock Runtime 不提供托管式网页搜索。如果你需要网页搜索，请使用 Mantle，并确认网关会保留工具请求和响应。</p> <p>另一种路由方式见 LiteLLM 的 <a href=\"https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers/bedrock_mantle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bedrock Mantle 集成（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>AWS 部署示例请参阅固定版本的 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai-on-aws/guidance-codex/blob/eb04fe0/docs/QUICKSTART_LLM_GATEWAY_LITELLM.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">LiteLLM on ECS 参考方案（需联网）</a>。该方案使用 Bedrock Runtime，并通过 ECS 任务角色刷新身份验证信息。请一并遵循其部署和身份验证步骤，并根据自己的网络、TLS、日志记录和资源保留政策审核其生产要求。</p> <p>无论选择哪种路由，都应根据<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a>验证已部署的网关版本、上游端点和模型组合。某个上游模型出现在网关模型列表中，并不能证明它与 Codex 配合时的流式传输、后续轮次和工具行为正常。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-a-runtime-model-route\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"runtime\">配置 Runtime 模型路由</h3> <p>将稳定的 Codex 别名映射到已批准的上游模型。使用下方 Runtime 示例前，请先确认你的 AWS 账户和区域中可以访问该模型。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">model_list:\n  - model_name: company-coding-model\n    litellm_params:\n      model: openai/global.openai.gpt-6-sol\n      api_key: os.environ/AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n      api_base: https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/openai/v1\n</code></pre> <p>请通过密钥管理系统将有效的 Bedrock API 密钥作为 <code>AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK</code> 提供。若密钥有效期较短，请在其到期前签发替代密钥、更新网关进程环境，并重启或重新部署使用该密钥的工作进程。ECS 参考方案则会从任务角色在进程内刷新凭据；请配套使用该方案的配置和入口程序。</p> <p><code>openai/</code> 前缀会选择 LiteLLM 的 OpenAI 兼容适配器；配置的 <code>api_base</code> 则会将请求发送到 Bedrock Runtime。Global 推理配置文件可能会把请求路由到源区域之外。请选择符合 AWS 权限和数据驻留要求的配置文件与区域，并按需替换示例中的两个值。</p> <p>客户端发送 <code>company-coding-model</code>，LiteLLM 使用已配置的上游路由。这个自定义别名需要下节说明的匹配客户端目录。通用网关不会自动获得内置 Bedrock 提供方的元数据调整。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-client-catalog\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">准备客户端模型目录</h3> <p>对于本 GPT-6 Sol/Runtime 示例和 Codex 0.158.0，请从对应版本的<a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.158.0/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">模型目录（需联网）</a>中获取完整的 <code>gpt-6-sol</code> 条目，并进行下表所列全部修改：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>字段</th> <th>必需修改</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>slug</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>\"company-coding-model\"</code>，与 LiteLLM 别名一致。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>visibility</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>\"list\"</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>availability_nux</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>null</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>upgrade</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>null</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>use_responses_lite</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>false</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>tool_mode</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>null</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>supported_reasoning_levels</code></td> <td>删除 <code>effort</code> 为 <code>\"ultra\"</code> 的条目；保留其他条目。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>additional_speed_tiers</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>[]</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>service_tiers</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>[]</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>default_service_tier</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>null</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>web_search_tool_type</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>\"text\"</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>multi_agent_version</code></td> <td>设置为 <code>\"v1\"</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>supports_search_tool</code></td> <td>对 Runtime 设置为 <code>false</code>。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>保留其他字段，包括模型指令和上下文长度限制。修改后的条目仍须放在目录顶层的 <code>models</code> 数组中。这些更改与已发布的 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.158.0/codex-rs/model-provider/src/amazon_bedrock/catalog.rs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bedrock 元数据调整（需联网）</a>和 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.158.0/codex-rs/model-provider/src/amazon_bedrock/runtime_catalog.rs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Runtime 搜索限制（需联网）</a>保持一致。更换客户端版本或上游模型时，请重新对照相应源码核实这些设置。</p> <p>分发完整 JSON 文件，并按照<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=supply-metadata-for-a-custom-alias\">部署网关</a>配置 <code>model_catalog_json</code>。在 Runtime 客户端配置中保留 <code>web_search = \"disabled\"</code>。向更多用户分发前，请先通过网关验证修改后的目录。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-responses-support\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"responses\">验证 Responses 支持</h3> <p>在面向客户端的 HTTPS 端点上提供 <code>POST /v1/responses</code>。配置负载均衡器和任何反向代理，使其转发流式事件时不进行缓冲。保留后续轮次和函数调用结果。仅有可用的 Chat Completions 端点，不足以满足此连接要求。</p> <p>分发客户端配置前，请完成<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a>中的检查。测试时应使用用户实际会采用的同一主机名、网络控制和身份验证路径。</p> <p><a id=\"issue-a-test-credential\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">签发测试凭据</h3> <p>为一名测试用户创建有作用范围限制的 LiteLLM 虚拟密钥。将其限制为已批准的别名，并配置到期时间、速率限制和预算。适用控制项请参阅 LiteLLM 的<a href=\"https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/proxy/virtual_keys\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">虚拟密钥文档（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>通过组织的密钥管理流程或身份验证辅助程序分发密钥。不要向用户提供 LiteLLM 管理密钥，也不要将网关凭据嵌入 <code>config.toml</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-the-user-connection\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">验证用户连接</h3> <p>扩大访问范围前，请完成以下检查：</p> <ol> <li>确认证书与网关主机名匹配，且服务健康。</li> <li>按照<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API／提供商凭据</a>为一名用户建立连接。</li> <li>运行一个简短提示词、一个后续轮次和一个只读工具任务。</li> <li>确认网关记录显示预期身份、别名和上游路由，并且没有泄露凭据或敏感提示词内容。</li> <li>测试凭据到期或撤销，并确认系统会拒绝未授权的模型别名。</li> </ol> <p>请在部署记录中保存已部署镜像的版本、路由配置和测试结果。团队分发和持续运维请继续参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">部署网关</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-the-connection\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">排查连接问题</h2> <p>请根据发生故障的层级缩小排查范围：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>现象</th> <th>检查内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>推理开始前 HTTPS 连接失败</td> <td>DNS、证书主机名、负载均衡器健康状态，以及允许的客户端网络。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>网关返回 <code>401</code> 或 <code>403</code></td> <td>结合网关日志，区分用户凭据被拒绝与上游 Bedrock 身份验证或权限失败。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>找不到所请求的模型</td> <td>确认客户端使用的精确别名，以及该别名映射的上游模型或推理配置文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>请求在到达 LiteLLM 前被拦截</td> <td>检查负载均衡器和 Web 应用防火墙日志，包括请求正文大小限制。测试有代表性的 Codex 请求时，仍要保留安全控制。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>文本能返回，但一个轮次无法完成</td> <td>检查流式缓冲、超时、终止事件，以及网关兼容性中的后续轮次和工具调用检查。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>上游请求超时</td> <td>检查源区域中的模型可用性、路由配置、配额和网关日志，再决定是否更改超时设置。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>修复后请沿用同一用户路径重新测试。网关健康检查成功，并不能证明经过身份验证的推理请求或完整 Codex 轮次也正常。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"bedrock-through-litellm\">Bedrock through LiteLLM</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use this page when your organization routes Codex to Amazon Bedrock through LiteLLM. If a LiteLLM gateway already exists, connect Codex first. Deploy LiteLLM only when your organization needs a new gateway.</p> <p>To use an existing gateway, start with <a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4?anchor=connect-to-an-existing-gateway\">Connect to an existing gateway</a>. To deploy LiteLLM on AWS, start with <a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4?anchor=prepare-a-gateway\">Prepare a gateway</a>. For access without a gateway, see <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">Amazon Bedrock</a>.</p> <p>Other gateway products follow the same <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">gateway requirements</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">API/provider connection flow</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-to-an-existing-gateway\">Connect to an existing gateway</h2> <p>Get these values from your gateway administrator:</p> <ul> <li>The HTTPS base URL, such as <code>https://gateway.example.com/v1</code>.</li> <li>The model alias that LiteLLM routes to an approved Bedrock model.</li> <li>The provider ID to use in Codex configuration.</li> <li>A scoped gateway credential or an authentication helper that returns it.</li> <li>Any model catalog distributed with your organization's configuration.</li> </ul> <p>Then complete the connection in this order:</p> <ol> <li>Ask your gateway team to confirm that the gateway serves <code>POST /v1/responses</code>, streams responses, preserves follow-up turns and tool calls, and routes the approved alias. See <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a>.</li> <li>Follow <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=configure-the-provider\">Use API/provider credentials</a> to configure the provider, model, and credential.</li> <li>Verify the active provider and alias, send the short <code>gateway-ok</code> prompt from the connection guide, and confirm that the LiteLLM record shows the expected user and alias.</li> <li>For organization-wide distribution, continue with <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">Roll out a gateway</a>.</li> </ol> <p>Your gateway credential authenticates you to LiteLLM. The gateway manages its own Bedrock credentials; you don't need to copy those credentials to your workstation.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-a-gateway\">Prepare a gateway</h2> <p>Use this section only when you need to create a LiteLLM gateway before connecting Codex.</p> <h3 id=\"before-you-deploy\">Before you deploy</h3> <p>Confirm that you have:</p> <ul> <li>Permission to deploy the approved LiteLLM architecture in your AWS environment.</li> <li>Bedrock access to the models or inference profiles you will route.</li> <li>A reviewed LiteLLM image and deployment pattern.</li> <li>A trusted HTTPS host name and certificate.</li> <li>A restricted client network range.</li> </ul> <p>For the Runtime example below, the gateway's AWS identity needs <code>bedrock:InvokeModel</code> for the selected inference profile and the account's default project. See AWS's <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-6-sol.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GPT-6 Sol setup instructions (online)</a> for the required permissions.</p> <h3 id=\"architecture\">Architecture</h3> <p>The deployment keeps LiteLLM between Codex and Bedrock, with HTTPS at the client boundary. The load balancer and LiteLLM are inside your organization's gateway boundary; the provider credential stays on the gateway.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex sends Responses API requests with a scoped gateway credential through an HTTPS load balancer to LiteLLM. LiteLLM routes the approved alias to Amazon Bedrock while the provider credential stays server-side. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/litellm-bedrock-architecture.svg\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex sends Responses API requests with a scoped gateway credential through an HTTPS load balancer to LiteLLM. LiteLLM routes the approved alias to Amazon Bedrock while the provider credential stays server-side. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/litellm-bedrock-architecture.svg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Restrict inbound access to approved clients, keep database and cache ports private, and grant the gateway only the Bedrock permissions it needs. Pin the deployed image by digest so that a restart doesn't silently change the implementation.</p> <p>Prompts, source excerpts, and tool results pass through the gateway and may enter its logs. Decide retention, access, and redaction before enabling request logging. MCP servers and plugins have separate connections and authentication; this gateway configuration doesn't configure them.</p> <h3 id=\"deployment-checkpoints\">Deployment checkpoints</h3> <p>Complete these checkpoints in order before handing the gateway to developers:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Checkpoint</th> <th>Output</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Deploy the proxy with private database and cache dependencies.</td> <td>A stable HTTPS base URL ending in <code>/v1</code>, with gateway-managed Bedrock authentication.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Configure a model route and its matching client catalog.</td> <td>A stable Codex-facing alias mapped to the intended Bedrock target.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Verify Responses support.</td> <td>A streamed <code>POST /v1/responses</code> response ending with <code>response.completed</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Issue a test credential.</td> <td>A per-user virtual key restricted to the alias, with expiration, budget, and rate limits.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Connect one developer.</td> <td>Codex provider configuration and a verified short prompt through the gateway.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The sections below cover each checkpoint. For production rollout, also test follow-up turns, tools, and credential revocation.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-the-bedrock-route\">Choose the Bedrock route</h3> <p>The LiteLLM upstream route determines the Bedrock endpoint, model identifier, and authentication method. Keep these choices together when you deploy or change the gateway.</p> <p>Use Bedrock Runtime for new configurations. The example below uses its OpenAI-compatible Responses endpoint.</p> <p>Hosted web search isn't available on Bedrock Runtime. If you need it, use Mantle and confirm that your gateway preserves the tool request and response.</p> <p>See LiteLLM's <a href=\"https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers/bedrock_mantle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bedrock Mantle integration (online)</a> for the alternative route.</p> <p>For an AWS deployment example, use the pinned <a href=\"https://github.com/openai-on-aws/guidance-codex/blob/eb04fe0/docs/QUICKSTART_LLM_GATEWAY_LITELLM.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">LiteLLM on ECS reference (online)</a>. That implementation uses Bedrock Runtime and refreshes authentication from the ECS task role. Follow its deployment and authentication steps together, and review its production requirements against your networking, TLS, logging, and resource-retention policies.</p> <p>Whichever route you choose, verify the deployed combination of gateway version, upstream endpoint, and model against <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a>. An upstream model appearing in the gateway's model list doesn't establish that its streaming, continuation, and tool behavior work with Codex.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-a-runtime-model-route\">Configure a Runtime model route</h3> <p>Map a stable Codex-facing alias to the approved upstream model. Confirm access in your AWS account and Region before using this Runtime example.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">model_list:\n  - model_name: company-coding-model\n    litellm_params:\n      model: openai/global.openai.gpt-6-sol\n      api_key: os.environ/AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n      api_base: https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/openai/v1\n</code></pre> <p>Supply a valid Bedrock API key as <code>AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK</code> through your secret-management system. For a short-lived key, issue a replacement before it expires, update the gateway process environment, and restart or redeploy the workers that use it. The ECS reference instead refreshes credentials in-process from its task role; use its configuration and entrypoint together.</p> <p>The <code>openai/</code> prefix selects LiteLLM's OpenAI-compatible adapter; the configured <code>api_base</code> sends requests to Bedrock Runtime. The Global inference profile can route requests outside the source Region. Choose a profile and Region that meet your AWS permissions and data-residency requirements, and replace both values as needed.</p> <p>The client sends <code>company-coding-model</code>; LiteLLM uses the configured upstream route. This custom alias requires the matching client catalog described next. A generic gateway does not inherit the built-in Bedrock provider's metadata adjustments.</p> <h3 id=\"prepare-the-client-catalog\">Prepare the client catalog</h3> <p>For this GPT-6 Sol/Runtime example with Codex 0.158.0, start with the complete <code>gpt-6-sol</code> entry from that version's <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.158.0/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">model catalog (online)</a>. Apply all of these edits to that entry:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Required edit</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>slug</code></td> <td>Set to <code>\"company-coding-model\"</code>, matching the LiteLLM alias.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>visibility</code></td> <td>Set to <code>\"list\"</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>availability_nux</code></td> <td>Set to <code>null</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>upgrade</code></td> <td>Set to <code>null</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>use_responses_lite</code></td> <td>Set to <code>false</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>tool_mode</code></td> <td>Set to <code>null</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>supported_reasoning_levels</code></td> <td>Remove the entry whose <code>effort</code> is <code>\"ultra\"</code>; retain the other entries.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>additional_speed_tiers</code></td> <td>Set to <code>[]</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>service_tiers</code></td> <td>Set to <code>[]</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>default_service_tier</code></td> <td>Set to <code>null</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>web_search_tool_type</code></td> <td>Set to <code>\"text\"</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>multi_agent_version</code></td> <td>Set to <code>\"v1\"</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>supports_search_tool</code></td> <td>Set to <code>false</code> for Runtime.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Preserve the remaining fields, including the model's instructions and context limits. Keep the edited entry in the catalog's top-level <code>models</code> array. These changes mirror the released <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.158.0/codex-rs/model-provider/src/amazon_bedrock/catalog.rs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bedrock metadata adjustments (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.158.0/codex-rs/model-provider/src/amazon_bedrock/runtime_catalog.rs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Runtime search restriction (online)</a>. Recheck them against the matching source when changing the client version or upstream model.</p> <p>Distribute the complete JSON file and configure <code>model_catalog_json</code> using <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=supply-metadata-for-a-custom-alias\">Roll out a gateway</a>. Keep <code>web_search = \"disabled\"</code> in the Runtime client configuration. Verify the edited catalog through the gateway before distributing it to more users.</p> <h3 id=\"verify-responses-support\">Verify Responses support</h3> <p>Expose <code>POST /v1/responses</code> at the client-facing HTTPS endpoint. Configure the load balancer and any reverse proxy to pass streaming events without buffering. Preserve follow-up turns and function-call results. A working Chat Completions endpoint alone isn't sufficient for this connection.</p> <p>Complete the checks in <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a> before distributing client configuration. Test through the same host name, network controls, and authentication path your users will use.</p> <h3 id=\"issue-a-test-credential\">Issue a test credential</h3> <p>Create a scoped LiteLLM virtual key for one test user. Restrict it to the approved alias and configure expiration, rate limits, and a budget. See LiteLLM's <a href=\"https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/proxy/virtual_keys\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">virtual-key documentation (online)</a> for the applicable controls.</p> <p>Distribute the key through your secret-management process or an authentication helper. Don't give users the LiteLLM administrative key or embed gateway credentials in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"verify-the-user-connection\">Verify the user connection</h3> <p>Complete these checks before expanding access:</p> <ol> <li>Confirm that the HTTPS certificate matches the gateway host name and the service is healthy.</li> <li>Connect one user through <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a>.</li> <li>Run a short prompt, a follow-up turn, and a read-only tool task.</li> <li>Confirm that gateway records show the expected identity, alias, and upstream route without exposing credentials or sensitive prompt content.</li> <li>Test credential expiration or revocation and confirm that unauthorized model aliases are rejected.</li> </ol> <p>Keep the deployed image version, route configuration, and test results with your rollout record. Continue with <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">Roll out a gateway</a> for team distribution and ongoing operations.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-the-connection\">Troubleshoot the connection</h2> <p>Use the failing layer to narrow the problem:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Symptom</th> <th>What to check</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>HTTPS fails before inference</td> <td>DNS, certificate host name, load-balancer health, and allowed client networks.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Gateway returns <code>401</code> or <code>403</code></td> <td>Distinguish a rejected user credential from an upstream Bedrock authentication or permission failure using gateway logs.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Requested model isn't found</td> <td>Confirm the exact client-facing alias and its upstream model or inference-profile mapping.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Request is blocked before reaching LiteLLM</td> <td>Check load-balancer and web application firewall logs, including request-body limits. Preserve your security controls while testing representative Codex requests.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Text works, but a turn doesn't finish</td> <td>Check streaming buffers, timeouts, terminal events, and the follow-up and tool-call checks in Gateway compatibility.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Upstream request times out</td> <td>Check model availability in the source Region, routing configuration, quotas, and gateway logs before changing timeouts.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Retest the same user path after a fix. A successful gateway health check doesn't verify an authenticated inference request or a complete Codex turn.</p>"};
